What is Beryllium Copper?

Beryllium Copper (BeCu) is an advanced copper alloy containing 0.2-2.7% beryllium, engineered for exceptional electrical conductivity, thermal stability, and fatigue resistance. The material has become indispensable in miniaturized electronic components including connectors, switches, MEMS devices, and RF components where reliability under stress is paramount. Its unique combination of properties makes it superior to conventional copper alloys in high-cycle applications.

